cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, the dataset or the trained model, please cite the article below."
title: "PECCD-Detect: a desktop application for automated multi-class detection of post-earthquake concrete defects"
type: software
version: "1.0.0"
license: AGPL-3.0-or-later
repository-code: "https://github.com/<your-account>/PECCD-Detect"
abstract: >-
  Standalone graphical application running the YOLOV12SDSDA detector trained on the
  Post-Earthquake Concrete Crack Dataset (PECCD). It localises and classifies six
  concrete deterioration mechanisms - scaling, spalling, multi-branched cracks, simple
  cracks, deep cracks and holes - in field photographs, and exports annotated images and
  quantitative damage reports.
keywords:
  - post-earthquake damage assessment
  - concrete defect detection
  - object detection
  - YOLO
  - structural health monitoring
  - quantitative nondestructive evaluation
